{"id": "EUVD-2026-103055", "enisaUuid": "7ae3a16a-b56f-3767-a810-d1e80f02f2d9", "description": "ZKEACMS through 4.4 contains an authentication bypass vulnerability that allows unauthenticated attackers to forge REST API JWT bearer tokens using a hard-coded HMAC-SHA256 signing key in JwtBearerDefaults.cs. Attackers can sign a token with the Name claim set to 'admin' to call ApiAuthorize endpoints, modifying articles and products and reading form submissions.", "datePublished": "2026-10-16T17:39:06", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T17:39:06", "baseScore": 8.8, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:L/VI:H/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@hieuPenguinnn/zkeacms-hardcoded-jwt-signing-key-admin-auth-bypass", "https://github.com/SeriaWei/ZKEACMS/blob/v4.4/src/ZKEACMS/Api/JwtBearerDefaults.cs#L14-L19", "https://github.com/SeriaWei/ZKEACMS/blob/v4.4/src/ZKEACMS/BuilderAuthentication.cs#L41-L52", "https://github.com/SeriaWei/ZKEACMS/issues/531", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/zkeacms-through-4.4-authentication-bypass-via-hard-coded-jwt-signing-key"], "aliases": ["GHSA-4v4h-58rp-w43w", "CVE-2026-111633"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.34, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "05e3cf70-ff99-3a7e-9324-40aff26de5d6", "product": {"name": "ZKEACMS", "vendor": {"name": "SeriaWei"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22644.4"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "6cf634bb-491d-3dd4-aa19-372eb244c387", "vendor": {"name": "SeriaWei"}}], "isExploited": false}